# data/ is versioned, deliberately, and this file is the record of why.
#
# It was ignored until 2026-08-13, on the reasoning that the .rds files are
# binaries that change completely on every rebuild and git would keep every
# version forever. That reasoning is sound and was outweighed.
#
# What outweighed it: these six files are the contract other people build
# against, and what they need from them is provenance - "which commit were
# these generated from?" - which git answers natively and a synced folder
# cannot. Shipping them out of band meant inventing a manifest to fake what a
# commit SHA already is.
#
# The cost, measured rather than guessed: about 6 MB a refresh, roughly 26 MB a
# year at four refreshes, against a .git already 93 MB. If the refresh cadence
# ever becomes weekly rather than a few times a year, revisit this - the two
# .rds files are binaries and store a full copy each time, while the four CSVs
# delta well.
#
# Nothing here is confidential: the survey data is published on Dataverse and
# the Shiny app is deployed publicly with these files bundled.
#
# Nothing is ignored in this directory on purpose. A seventh output file added
# later should be tracked without anyone remembering to allow it - which is the
# failure that kept 09_create_dashboard_data.R out of git entirely. OS junk is
# handled by the repository root .gitignore.
